<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Nightly / pre-release (Pre) entitlements.

	  Deliberately omits com.apple.security.app-sandbox. CodeEdit's integrated
	  terminal runs a real interactive login shell, and under the App Sandbox that
	  shell cannot read the user's dotfiles, cannot setpgid() for job control, and
	  taints every subprocess it spawns (e.g. `xcrun` refuses to run at all inside a
	  sandbox). Shipping a sandboxed terminal produces:

	      zsh: operation not permitted: /Users/<user>/.zprofile
	      zsh: can't set tty pgrp: operation not permitted
	      zsh: locking failed for ~/.zsh_history: operation not permitted
	      xcrun: error: cannot be used within an App Sandbox.

	  The Alpha/Beta/Release configurations keep the sandbox, because they ship to
	  the App Store / are notarized. Only the Pre (nightly) configuration uses this
	  file, so the sandboxed shipping configuration stays intact.

	  Retained from the sandboxed entitlements: file access needed by the editor.
	  Dropped: app-sandbox, application-groups and app-scope bookmarks, all of which
	  are sandbox concepts and would be meaningless or invalid without a team ID.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.network.client</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
